      "writtenOn": "2026-08-04T17:56:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "MKL Sparse QR decomposition is not rank-revealing. It looks like even setting [`mkl_sparse_set_qr_hint`](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/docs/onemkl/developer-reference-c/2025-2/mkl-sparse-set-qr-hint.html) to `SPARSE_QR_WITH_PIVOTS` reports success in case of a Jacobian with all zeros column while returning NaNs.\n\nA possible option is a post-hoc finiteness/non-negativity test.",
      "parentUuid": "14535603_94652012",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 585,
        "startChar": 44,
        "endLine": 585,
        "endChar": 58
      },
      "revId": "c550c515d19fb87cc92aefe6c21f4192a70c586b",
